invariant reading
1. Shell-1 status is a gate, not a scalar. Damaged rows should route
   through HYP-2661 before far residual estimates are invoked.
2. The p1-tax inequality is the far-side boundary currency. In this
   bounded bank, coefficients up to c=3/8 are tested after splitting by shell-1 packet.
3. The proof order is two-gate: shell-1 conservation first, then p1
   boundary tax for the remaining shell-1-full or nonlocal rows.

Tournament Analysis
  vertices: shell1_gate, p1_boundary_tax, missing_packet, cap_slack, raw_value
  observable: preservation of p0+(1/7+c)p1 <= cap9 through c=3/8
  switch/gauge: split by shell-1 missing packet before scalarizing p1 tax
  Hamiltonian path: shell1_gate > p1_boundary_tax > missing_packet > cap_slack > raw_value
  challenged assumption: far Delta and AP-tail shell gates are separate; they are two gauges of boundary currency.
